# Gallery persistence (hard rule)

Prints live in `Documents/polaroids` under bundle id `com.postcardfilm.app`.

**While the app stays installed, the gallery must never be wiped** — not by TestFlight, App Store updates, Xcode Run, Debug vs Release, or any git branch (`test` / `main` / `release`). Uninstall (or changing the bundle id) is the only full loss iOS allows. In-app delete after the confirm modal is the only allowed intentional delete.

## Never

- `FileManager.removeItem` on the polaroids **root** (`Documents/polaroids`).
- Replace `index.json` with seed-only rows that drop real UUID prints.
- Change `PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER` / `com.postcardfilm.app` casually (a new id is a new app).
- Put `-SCREENSHOTS` on a scheme used to **Run on a physical phone**.

## Screenshot harness

- Compile only under `#if DEBUG && targetEnvironment(simulator)`.
- Seed may upsert / refresh folders whose ids start with `seed-` only.
- Index updates must go through `PolaroidIndexLogic.mergingScreenshotSeeds` (keep every non-`seed-` record).
- Never delete UUID print folders from the harness.

## Store

- [`PolaroidStore`](PostcardFilm/Store/PolaroidStore.swift) may `removeItem` only a **per-print** directory from `delete(id:)` / `delete(ids:)` after UI confirm.
- Keep `repairIndexFromDisk` / `recoverMissingRecords` so folders with `polaroid.png` reappear if the index is thin.

## Tests / docs

- [`GalleryPersistenceTests`](PostcardFilmTests/GalleryPersistenceTests.swift) must stay green.
- Human copy: README **Gallery persistence**, [`docs/BRANCHING.md`](docs/BRANCHING.md), HIG Identity, FEATURE_COVERAGE, DESIGN Brand.
